ascii-garden by Ridit (https://github.com/ridit-jangra/ascii-garden)

The lyrics garden mode ("6") is a direct port of the rendering
algorithms of ascii-garden at revision
f519e85f12a8e47b6c7b73a0d13a85043dedbc40: the role/coverage
classifier, glyph families, subpixel mask rasterization, letter
layout and wrap, stem/leaf/rose geometry and growth parameters, sway
and the "Paper" palette, adapted from Canvas to terminal cells as
documented in docs/PORT-PLAN.md. ascii-garden is itself a
reinterpretation of Akshat Agarwal's Type Garden, and its cell-grid
ASCII approach is adapted from ascii-animals by drewdi /
DesignerStephen1; those works keep their own licences and copyrights.
The garden's type is the genuine Playfair Display font (see below),
as in the reference. No Type Garden assets were used.

